& [JustificationRecord: ChatWorkbenchSourceReveal: 2026-05-14] is the justification for source reveal edge-state hardening
  + [justification_uuid] is 8a4552f7-16dc-4e45-9496-20c493a4730f
  + [work_uuid] is 90b49354-b353-4d4f-9c38-d6e417d8562a
  + [specification_anchor] is [ImplementationFrontier: ChatRefinementV2] frontier_4
  + [requirement] is make editing-line source reveal robust for active cuts, removed cuts, missing source blocks, and hidden panes
  + [fork_commit] is d893072f
  + [solution] is removed cuts are now fetched, shown in a dedicated Cutting details region, and included in raw debug state
  + [solution] is missing source blocks render as explicit stale-source text instead of raw IDs that look valid
  + [solution] is reveal status now distinguishes active cut reveal, removed cut reveal, missing source block, hidden Chat pane, and hidden Cutting pane
  + [solution] is runtime proof markers now assert removed-cut and stale-source UI strings/classes
  + [data_design_reason] is removed cuts remain derivative evidence and are not erased from the refinement interaction model
  + [ui_interaction_reason] is source navigation failures become visible recovery information instead of silent scroll misses

  = must: keep removed cuts inspectable without restoring them implicitly
  = must: keep stale source state visually distinct from valid source text
  = must: preserve source reveal as navigation, not mutation

